            <ArticleTitle>Left coronary to right ventricle fistula in a child: management strategy based on cardiac-gated 64-slice CT.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>325-7</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Congenital coronary fistulae are a diagnostic challenge. A prerequisite for best management is accurate anatomical evaluation, traditionally provided by invasive catheter angiography. Multislice CT (MSCT) is an emerging noninvasive technique for coronary artery evaluation. We present a 3-year-old boy and highlight the clinical usefulness of new-generation MSCT to study coronary artery fistulae in children. Multiplanar and 3-D reconstruction offer invaluable information to plan the best therapeutic strategy in this setting. We provide evidence for the expanding clinical role of MSCT for coronary artery imaging in children.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
